The family’s solver-facing problem is an exact cover over indexed 3-sets, even though the paper supplies the split-graph list-coloring interpretation. I’ll classify it accordingly and mark the Section 5, Lemma 5 reduction honestly: the generator restricts the arbitrary Independent Set graph to a regular 3-uniform intersection graph and emits only the compact low-color witness. The candidate sampler and `search_space` already agree semantically on uniform unordered size-`n` subsets, so neither needs a behavioral change.
