The fresh shipping run found 0 valid candidates in 200,000 uniform samples at `n=40, degree=5`. On that same shipping instance, min-column Algorithm X reached its 10,000-node cap after visiting 10,001 nodes in 0.06384158786386251 seconds and returned no verified witness. That is sparse by the sampled measure, but computationally cheap as a capped failure, so I’m recording both facts and keeping the caveat explicit.
